---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Shipping"
  description="How AIB Robot ships: US and EU warehouse availability is reconfirmed before payment. We do not publish a delivery-day range we have not confirmed. Packaging is requested discreet. We do not misdeclare customs."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="kicker">Shipping</p>
      <h1>What we can actually promise.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Stock, price, and the packing method are confirmed before you pay. A delivery-day range is not, until we have a current figure for the unit in question.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose" style="padding-bottom:4.5rem">
      <h2>US warehouse</h2>
      <p>
        Companion figures on our <a href="/in-stock-us">US warehouse</a> page are taken from the US warehouse lists we received in November 2026. We will ask whether a specific unit is still there — and confirm the head, skin, and material actually available — before we ask you to pay. If it is, shipment from a US warehouse is usually faster than a figure that still has to be made. How many days it will take is something we will tell you for that unit, once we know. We do not publish a delivery-day range or a unit count.
      </p>
      <h2>EU warehouse</h2>
      <p>
        A smaller set of bodies appears on the EU warehouse list we received in November 2026; those figures are on our <a href="/in-stock-eu">EU warehouse</a> page. The same rule applies: we reconfirm whether a unit is still there before payment, and we do not publish a delivery-day range or a unit count.
      </p>
      <h2>Figures that are made to order</h2>
      <p>
        Figures that are not on the November 2026 US or EU warehouse lists, including the AI expression head, are available to order. Lead time is confirmed in writing before payment. We do not copy a production estimate onto your order until we have a current confirmation for your configuration.
      </p>
      <h2>Discreet packaging</h2>
      <p>
        We request unmarked outer packaging — a plain carton, without product photography or a product name on the outside. We will confirm the packing method with your order. We cannot control how a carrier describes a package in its own tracking, and we will not pretend that no one can ever infer the contents.
      </p>
      <h2>Customs and prohibited destinations</h2>
      <p>
        We will not misdeclare the contents of a shipment. We will not describe a companion figure as a mannequin, a toy, or any other inaccurate category in order to clear customs, including any Mid-East or other grey-customs arrangement. If a destination prohibits the import of these products, we will not ship there. You are responsible for knowing the law where the package will be received. Duties, taxes, and clearance formalities, where they apply, are for the recipient unless we have agreed otherwise in writing.
      </p>
      <p>
        See also our <a href="/compliance">compliance</a> page.
      </p>
      <h2>Cost</h2>
      <p>
        The prices on product pages are the figure prices, not a freight quote. The shipping cost for your order is confirmed before payment, once we know the warehouse, the destination, and the weight of the actual unit.
      </p>
      <h2>Inspection on arrival</h2>
      <p>
        When the carton arrives, inspect the outer packaging and, as soon as you reasonably can, the figure itself. If there is transit damage or a factory defect, write to us with photographs. The remedy is described on the <a href="/returns">returns</a> page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
